From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Dichev <stefanbdichev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:25:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] core: end key requests on shutdown, and drop a reconnect
 nobody holds

A shutdown that raced the start of a reconnect could leave the audio-key
manager holding requests for a reconnect that never completes. The
manager now takes no requests once its session is shut down, as Mercury
does, so none can wait after a shutdown in either order.

The connection task checks the session again after the reconnect, so a
session shut down or dropped meanwhile neither takes over the new
connection nor caches its credentials. A reconnect no longer resends key
requests whose callers stopped waiting. Every wait in the key tests is
bounded, and the login timeout's comment no longer claims the TCP
connect, which happens outside it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zyp13aMbmU4XmKnuCPVRb
(cherry picked from commit 14c86372f99e08b59ea68fe4bfa1cb5ee3be5993)
